		<div class=3D"fl-rich-text">
	<p>Deburring is crucial in the metalworking process, ensuring safe and usa=
ble part generation. Many metal machining processes, such as milling, grind=
ing, drilling and stamping, leave sharp, raised edges, ridges and protrusio=
ns <a href=3D"https://timesaversinc.com/blog/what-is-deburring-2/">known as=
 burs</a> behind. Metal deburring machines are&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://time=
saversinc.com/blog/what-is-deburring/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener no=
referrer">designed to remove these imperfections</a>&nbsp;from machined met=
al products to create a smooth, high-quality finish. At Timesavers, we use =
extensive research and customer feedback to develop automated deburring mac=
hines that deliver a superior surface finish. We've served as leading debur=
ring machine manufacturers since 1946, producing innovative products design=
ed to boost production speeds while minimizing labor costs.</p>
</div>
